# Real HTTP response headers.
#
# GitHub Pages ignores this file entirely - it cannot send custom headers.
# Cloudflare Pages and Netlify read it from the publish directory and send
# these as actual headers. That distinction is the whole point of this file:
#
#   frame-ancestors   CANNOT be delivered by a <meta> tag (CSP spec excludes
#                     it), so until the site moves host, clickjacking is not
#                     prevented. This file is the fix.
#   HSTS              likewise impossible via meta.
#
# The meta CSP in index.html stays as defence in depth for however the file is
# served. Header CSP and meta CSP are intersected, so this file deliberately
# restates ONLY frame-ancestors rather than the full policy - duplicating the
# policy in two places is how the two drift apart and start blocking something
# that works.
#
# HSTS is one day on purpose. includeSubDomains and preload are separate,
# much harder-to-reverse decisions, and this brand does not take those on
# someone else's domain without asking.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=86400
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
